    This section examines the overall trajectory of intentional homicide rates from 1990 to {most_recent_year},
    using both the median and mean homicide rate across reporting countries. The median is the preferred
    central-tendency measure because it is resistant to extreme values — a small number of countries with
    very high rates can inflate the mean substantially.
