<!-- ─── SECTION 3: GENDER DISPARITY ─────────────────────────────────────── -->
<div class="section" id="sex-disparity">
  <h2>3. Gender Disparity in Homicide Victimization</h2>

  <p>
    Homicide is a highly gendered phenomenon. Globally, men are far more likely to be victims
    of intentional homicide than women, though the magnitude of this disparity varies considerably
    across countries and cultural contexts. Understanding this gap is critical for designing
    targeted prevention strategies.
  </p>

  <div class="kpi-grid">
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-value" style="color: {COLORS['male']}">{male_all[male_all['year'] >= 2015].groupby('year')['homicide_rate'].median().median():.1f}</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Median Male Rate (2015+)</div>
