    <li><strong>Magnitude:</strong> In the most recent year with comprehensive data, men were approximately {latest_mf_ratio:.1f} times more likely to be homicide victims than women, globally.</li>
    <li><strong>Context matters:</strong> While the ratio reflects higher male victimization overall, this does not diminish the significance of female homicide — in many contexts, women are disproportionately killed by intimate partners or family members, a pattern often obscured by aggregate statistics.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="chart-container">
