    <li><strong>Invest in youth violence prevention:</strong> The 15–29 age group faces homicide rates far exceeding other demographics. Evidence-based programs — including early childhood interventions, school-based violence prevention, and employment programs for at-risk youth — should be scaled.</li>
    <li><strong>Address gender-specific dynamics:</strong> While men represent the majority of homicide victims, violence against women — particularly intimate partner and family-related homicide — requires distinct prevention strategies. Gender-disaggregated data collection should be expanded.</li>
