    <li><strong>Learn from success stories:</strong> Countries that have achieved dramatic reductions in homicide — such as those identified in Section 5 — offer valuable case studies. Systematic documentation and cross-country learning should be facilitated.</li>
    <li><strong>Guard against reversals:</strong> The data shows that security gains can be fragile. Sustained investment is needed even after improvements are achieved, and early-warning systems should be developed to detect deteriorations before they escalate.</li>
